          "hideComponent": "false",
          "topMargin": "7",
          "jcr:created": "Wed Nov 27 2024 14:28:12 GMT+0000",
          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "text": "<h3><span class=\"futura-bold\">Inspiring the next generation of environmental stewards&nbsp;</span></h3>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Nov 27 2024 14:43:39 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        },
        "text": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "user-7a617b9e44@example.invalid",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-7a617b9e44@example.invalid",
          "jcr:created": "Wed Nov 27 2024 14:28:41 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Families played a significant role in this year's event, with many employees bringing their children to join in the planting effort. It’s a chance not only to get their hands dirty but also to learn about the importance of preserving the environment for the future. “Seeing the kids out here, excited to plant ‘their’ tree, really brings home the idea that we’re doing something that matters,” said Jan Sahm, Staff Project Specialist Quality Operations and SEA site lead. “We’re not just teaching them about trees; we’re teaching them how to care for the world around them.”</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">The sight of children alongside their parents, shovels in hand, was one of the most inspiring aspects of the day. It’s clear that these events are fostering a sense of responsibility and connection to the environment that will last far beyond the planting. “It was great to see the next generation getting involved,” said Ecklund. “We’re creating lifelong memories and values for these kids.”</span></p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Nov 27 2024 14:29:04 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      },
